<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's seven months energy demand up 10 pct.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's seven months energy demand up 10 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's energy demand rose 10 percent to 93.26 million tonnes of oil equivalent (TOE) in the first seven months of 1996 from 84.77 million a year ago, the Ministry of Trade, Industry and Energy said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Energy consumption grew thanks to increasing use of liquefied natural gas (LNG) for home fuel and hydroelectric power, a ministry statement said.</p>
<p>Oil products demand growth slowed, however, pressured by an industrial slowdown, it said.  </p>
<p>Breakdown of South Korea's demand for energy resources in the first seven months, compared with the same period last year.</p>
<p>(Figures in brackets are year-on-year growth in percentage):</p>
<p>				Jan-July 1996	 Jan-July 1995</p>
<p>				Amount		  Amount</p>
<p> Total			93,257  (10.0)	84,769   (9.7)</p>
<p>(in 1,000 TOE)</p>
<p> Petroleum products    411,985   (7.4)     383,528   (9.4)</p>
<p>(in 1,000 barrels)</p>
<p> LNG			   5,292  (32.8)	 3,984  (21.2)</p>
<p>(in 1,000 tonnes)  </p>
<p> Hard coal		   2,429 (-16.0)	 2,892 (-24.2)</p>
<p>(in 1,000 tonnes)</p>
<p> Bituminous coal	  24,288  (11.7)	21,746  (11.8)</p>
<p>(in 1,000 tonnes)</p>
<p> Nuclear power	    42,826  (12.8)	37,971  (11.0)</p>
<p>(in gigawatt hours)</p>
<p> Hydroelectric power     3,156  (22.0)	 2,586  (-3.7)</p>
<p>(in gigawatt hours)</p>
<p> Other			   654  (10.4)	   592  (16.0)</p>
<p>(in 1,000 TOE)</p>
<p>(Source: Ministry of Trade, Industry and Energy).</p>
